"use strict";(self.webpackChunkspa_template=self.webpackChunkspa_template||[]).push([[590],{8590:s=>{s.exports=JSON.parse('{"created":"2018-11-23T12:05:00","modified":"2018-11-23T12:05:00","id":1041,"title":"Javascript Async/Await - Use New Shiny Responsibly","article":"<p>The Async and Await keywords are a great addition to the language and can really help make clean code, and I see more and more instances of people using them. </p>\\n<p>This article is not going to say dont use them, its not even just about async/await, its about being conscious of what you are using and any trade off&#39;s that occur.</p>\\n<h2 id=\\"tldr\\">TL;DR</h2>\\n<p>Only use async/await when targeting the latest browsers/platforms and compiling/bundling your javascript. Otherwise use simple Promises to avoid a large generated overhead in your bundle for every async method. Unless you arent concerned with a large initial bundle size of course.</p>\\n<h2 id=\\"the-trade-off\\">The Trade Off</h2>\\n<p>In the frontend world we often need to transpile/compile our code to be able to reach and work on older browsers/platforms, this can result in generated code and polyfills used to replicate those features. However we also are attempting to make first load a quick process, to prevent users leaving, but also to reduce server payloads etc, so it is often useful to know what your code is compiling too.</p>\\n<p>This can lead to to a trade off, between compatibility, a fast initial page load or the decision to create multiple output builds (one for new platforms and one for legacy).</p>\\n<h3 id=\\"asyncawait-example\\">Async/Await example</h3>\\n<p>Below is the very simple example of an async function.</p>\\n<p><strong>NB</strong> All these examples can easily be replicated by the <a href=\\"https://babeljs.io/en/repl\\">online babel repl</a> which I highly recommend as a scratchpad to see how things are &#39;compiled&#39;.</p>\\n<pre><code class=\\"hljs language-js\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">const</span> myFunc = <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">async</span> () =&gt; <span class=\\"hljs-built_in\\">Promise</span>.resolve(<span class=\\"hljs-number\\">1</span>);\\n<span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">const</span> myFunc2 = <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">async</span> () =&gt; <span class=\\"hljs-built_in\\">Promise</span>.resolve(<span class=\\"hljs-number\\">2</span>);</code></pre>\\n<p>If targeting a modern browser, Ill use the latest chrome <code>last 1 Chrome versions</code> the output would look almost the same:</p>\\n<pre><code class=\\"hljs language-js\\"><span class=\\"hljs-comment\\">// latest chrome</span>\\n<span class=\\"hljs-meta\\">\\"use strict\\"</span>;\\n\\n<span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">const</span> myFunc = <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">async</span> () =&gt; <span class=\\"hljs-built_in\\">Promise</span>.resolve(<span class=\\"hljs-number\\">1</span>);\\n<span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">const</span> myFunc2 = <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">async</span> () =&gt; <span class=\\"hljs-built_in\\">Promise</span>.resolve(<span class=\\"hljs-number\\">2</span>);</code></pre>\\n<p>Not a problem right? And if we look at <a href=\\"https://caniuse.com/#feat=async-functions\\">caniuse - async functions</a> a large amount of &#39;evergreen&#39; browsers do support async/await out the box, awesome.</p>\\n<h2 id=\\"recent-legacy-platform-support\\">Recent Legacy Platform Support</h2>\\n<p>Often though we arent just developing for the newest browsers though and we need to factor in older browsers as well.</p>\\n<p>So lets take a small step back from the latest browsers and look at chrome 54 <code>chrome &gt;= 54, firefox &gt;= 53</code>:</p>\\n<pre><code class=\\"hljs language-js\\"><span class=\\"hljs-comment\\">// chrome 54+ firefox 53+</span>\\n<span class=\\"hljs-meta\\">\\"use strict\\"</span>;\\n\\n<span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> <span class=\\"hljs-title\\">_asyncToGenerator</span>(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\">fn</span>) </span>{\\n    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> <span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> (<span class=\\"hljs-params\\"></span>) </span>{\\n        <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">var</span> gen = fn.apply(<span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">this</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-built_in\\">arguments</span>);\\n        <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">new</span> <span class=\\"hljs-built_in\\">Promise</span>(<span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> (<span class=\\"hljs-params\\">resolve, reject</span>) </span>{\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> <span class=\\"hljs-title\\">step</span>(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\">key, arg</span>) </span>{\\n                <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">try</span> {\\n                    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">var</span> info = gen[key](arg);\\n                    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">var</span> value = info.value;\\n                } <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">catch</span> (error) {\\n                    reject(error);\\n                    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span>;\\n                }\\n                <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">if</span> (info.done) {\\n                    resolve(value);\\n                } <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">else</span> {\\n                    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> <span class=\\"hljs-built_in\\">Promise</span>.resolve(value).then(<span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> (<span class=\\"hljs-params\\">value</span>) </span>{\\n                        step(<span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"next\\"</span>, value);\\n                    }, <span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> (<span class=\\"hljs-params\\">err</span>) </span>{\\n                        step(<span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"throw\\"</span>, err);\\n                    });\\n                }\\n            }\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> step(<span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"next\\"</span>);\\n        });\\n    };\\n}\\n\\n<span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">const</span> myFunc = <span class=\\"hljs-function\\">(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\">(</span>) =&gt;</span> {\\n  <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">var</span> _ref = _asyncToGenerator(<span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span>* (<span class=\\"hljs-params\\"></span>) </span>{\\n    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> <span class=\\"hljs-built_in\\">Promise</span>.resolve(<span class=\\"hljs-number\\">1</span>);\\n  });\\n\\n  <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> <span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> <span class=\\"hljs-title\\">myFunc</span>(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\"></span>) </span>{\\n    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> _ref.apply(<span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">this</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-built_in\\">arguments</span>);\\n  };\\n})();\\n\\n<span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">const</span> myFunc2 = <span class=\\"hljs-function\\">(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\">(</span>) =&gt;</span> {\\n  <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">var</span> _ref2 = _asyncToGenerator(<span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span>* (<span class=\\"hljs-params\\"></span>) </span>{\\n    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> <span class=\\"hljs-built_in\\">Promise</span>.resolve(<span class=\\"hljs-number\\">2</span>);\\n  });\\n\\n  <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> <span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> <span class=\\"hljs-title\\">myFunc2</span>(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\"></span>) </span>{\\n    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> _ref2.apply(<span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">this</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-built_in\\">arguments</span>);\\n  };\\n})();</code></pre>\\n<p>Wow whats happened there? Well only the latest browsers support async/await. If a browser can support <a href=\\"https://caniuse.com/#feat=es6-generators\\">generator* functions</a> then babel will attempt to create a helper function <code>_asyncToGenerator</code> to simulate async/await and although its a lot more code its only one extra function and only simple wrapper functions with Promises around each async function. Not good but acceptable.</p>\\n<h3 id=\\"real-world-legacy-platform-support\\">Real World Legacy Platform Support</h3>\\n<p>The problem is very few browsers supported generators for long before async functions and in the real world there is still a large share of users using older browsers that cant, with IE 11 being the prime example; <a href=\\"https://www.w3counter.com/globalstats.php?year=2018&amp;month=10\\">global stats - 2.87%</a> <a href=\\"http://gs.statcounter.com/browser-market-share#monthly-201807-201810\\">statista 2.88%</a>. </p>\\n<p><em><strong>NB</strong> Although you might think but try persuading a manager you want to dump 28,800 customers from your 1,000,000 customer base, purely because you want to use the &#39;new shiny&#39; thing in dev?</em></p>\\n<p>Also when dealing with business customers, regularly they would be using desktop browsers specifically and only what a infrastructure engineer has installed for them, in the desktop only category IE has a higher usage level, in some reports as high as 10% <a href=\\"https://netmarketshare.com/browser-market-share.aspx?options=%7B%22filter%22%3A%7B%22%24and%22%3A%5B%7B%22deviceType%22%3A%7B%22%24in%22%3A%5B%22Desktop%2Flaptop%22%5D%7D%7D%5D%7D%2C%22dateLabel%22%3A%22Custom%22%2C%22attributes%22%3A%22share%22%2C%22group%22%3A%22browser%22%2C%22sort%22%3A%7B%22share%22%3A-1%7D%2C%22id%22%3A%22browsersDesktop%22%2C%22dateInterval%22%3A%22Monthly%22%2C%22dateStart%22%3A%222018-07%22%2C%22dateEnd%22%3A%222018-10%22%2C%22segments%22%3A%22-1000%22%7D\\">netmarketshare</a></p>\\n<p>So what does the output for IE 11 and also chrome 48 and below <code>chrome &gt; 46, ie &gt; 11</code> look like? </p>\\n<pre><code class=\\"hljs language-js\\"><span class=\\"hljs-meta\\">\\"use strict\\"</span>;\\n\\n<span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> <span class=\\"hljs-title\\">_asyncToGenerator</span>(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\">fn</span>) </span>{\\n    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> <span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> (<span class=\\"hljs-params\\"></span>) </span>{\\n        <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">var</span> gen = fn.apply(<span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">this</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-built_in\\">arguments</span>);\\n        <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">new</span> <span class=\\"hljs-built_in\\">Promise</span>(<span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> (<span class=\\"hljs-params\\">resolve, reject</span>) </span>{\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> <span class=\\"hljs-title\\">step</span>(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\">key, arg</span>) </span>{\\n                <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">try</span> {\\n                    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">var</span> info = gen[key](arg);\\n                    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">var</span> value = info.value;\\n                } <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">catch</span> (error) {\\n                    reject(error);\\n                    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span>;\\n                }\\n                <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">if</span> (info.done) {\\n                    resolve(value);\\n                } <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">else</span> {\\n                    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> <span class=\\"hljs-built_in\\">Promise</span>.resolve(value).then(<span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> (<span class=\\"hljs-params\\">value</span>) </span>{\\n                        step(<span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"next\\"</span>, value);\\n                    }, <span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> (<span class=\\"hljs-params\\">err</span>) </span>{\\n                        step(<span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"throw\\"</span>, err);\\n                    });\\n                }\\n            }\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> step(<span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"next\\"</span>);\\n        });\\n    };\\n}\\n\\n<span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">var</span> myFunc = <span class=\\"hljs-function\\">(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\">(</span>) =&gt;</span> {\\n    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">var</span> _ref = _asyncToGenerator( <span class=\\"hljs-comment\\">/*#__PURE__*/</span> regeneratorRuntime.mark(<span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> <span class=\\"hljs-title\\">_callee</span>(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\"></span>) </span>{\\n        <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> regeneratorRuntime.wrap(<span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> <span class=\\"hljs-title\\">_callee$</span>(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\">_context</span>) </span>{\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">while</span> (<span class=\\"hljs-number\\">1</span>) {\\n                <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">switch</span> (_context.prev = _context.next) {\\n                    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">case</span> <span class=\\"hljs-number\\">0</span>:\\n                        <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> _context.abrupt(<span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"return\\"</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-built_in\\">Promise</span>.resolve(<span class=\\"hljs-number\\">1</span>));\\n\\n                    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">case</span> <span class=\\"hljs-number\\">1</span>:\\n                    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">case</span> <span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"end\\"</span>:\\n                        <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> _context.stop();\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }, _callee, <span class=\\"hljs-literal\\">undefined</span>);\\n    }));\\n\\n    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> <span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> <span class=\\"hljs-title\\">myFunc</span>(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\"></span>) </span>{\\n        <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> _ref.apply(<span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">this</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-built_in\\">arguments</span>);\\n    };\\n})();\\n\\n<span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">var</span> myFunc2 = <span class=\\"hljs-function\\">(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\">(</span>) =&gt;</span> {\\n    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">var</span> _ref2 = _asyncToGenerator( <span class=\\"hljs-comment\\">/*#__PURE__*/</span> regeneratorRuntime.mark(<span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> <span class=\\"hljs-title\\">_callee2</span>(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\"></span>) </span>{\\n        <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> regeneratorRuntime.wrap(<span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> <span class=\\"hljs-title\\">_callee2$</span>(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\">_context2</span>) </span>{\\n            <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">while</span> (<span class=\\"hljs-number\\">1</span>) {\\n                <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">switch</span> (_context2.prev = _context2.next) {\\n                    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">case</span> <span class=\\"hljs-number\\">0</span>:\\n                        <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> _context2.abrupt(<span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"return\\"</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-built_in\\">Promise</span>.resolve(<span class=\\"hljs-number\\">2</span>));\\n\\n                    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">case</span> <span class=\\"hljs-number\\">1</span>:\\n                    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">case</span> <span class=\\"hljs-string\\">\\"end\\"</span>:\\n                        <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> _context2.stop();\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }, _callee2, <span class=\\"hljs-literal\\">undefined</span>);\\n    }));\\n\\n    <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> <span class=\\"hljs-function\\"><span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">function</span> <span class=\\"hljs-title\\">myFunc2</span>(<span class=\\"hljs-params\\"></span>) </span>{\\n        <span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">return</span> _ref2.apply(<span class=\\"hljs-keyword\\">this</span>, <span class=\\"hljs-built_in\\">arguments</span>);\\n    };\\n})();\\n</code></pre>\\n<p>Now this is much worse, not only is there a <code>_asyncToGenerator</code> method and a complete <code>regeneratorRuntime</code> global package thats been imported but for every single async method you create an extra 18 lines of code and a nested paradise of closures await (yeah it&#39;s a bad pun lol). Worse still is that is every method now has a forever running while loop inside of it waiting for a result to be generated.</p>\\n<h3 id=\\"creating-a-library\\">Creating a library</h3>\\n<p>Its not just those that are targeting old browsers that need to be aware of their choices. </p>\\n<p>Now imagine you are creating a library for someone to use (open source or internal to the company isnt important) you also have no idea what your consumer will be using it for. So you use babel (possibly with webpack) to bundle it for the consumer, but you keep your browser support as high a coverage as you can to reach more consumers, but unwittingly create the same problem as above.</p>\\n<h3 id=\\"thank-you-to-the-babel-team\\">Thank you to the Babel Team</h3>\\n<p>I dont want this to seem like I am bashing babel and the amazing work they do. The decisions they have made with regards to this generated code makes perfect sense, simulate async/await with generators, then simulate generators if not available with inline code and a runtime library. </p>\\n<p>Please give them support as they make all our lives as developers easier and in many case make companies productive enough to survive. #SpreadTheLove :)</p>\\n<h2 id=\\"summary\\">Summary</h2>\\n<p>Use await and async, but use them knowing your target is able to accept async/await natively or at least generators natively. Otherwise stick to using Promises in your code, despite issues people have raised with Promises they are not difficult to write and consume. And can easily be polyfilled if your environment doesnt support them.</p>\\n<h2 id=\\"references\\">References</h2>\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\"https://babeljs.io/en/repl\\">babel repl</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\"https://caniuse.com/#feat=async-functions\\">caniuse - async functions</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\"https://caniuse.com/#feat=es6-generators\\">caniuse - generator* functions</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\"http://gs.statcounter.com/browser-market-share#monthly-201807-201810\\">Statista</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\"https://www.w3counter.com/globalstats.php?year=2018&amp;month=10\\">Global Stats</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\"https://netmarketshare.com/browser-market-share.aspx?options=%7B%22filter%22%3A%7B%22%24and%22%3A%5B%7B%22deviceType%22%3A%7B%22%24in%22%3A%5B%22Desktop%2Flaptop%22%5D%7D%7D%5D%7D%2C%22dateLabel%22%3A%22Custom%22%2C%22attributes%22%3A%22share%22%2C%22group%22%3A%22browser%22%2C%22sort%22%3A%7B%22share%22%3A-1%7D%2C%22id%22%3A%22browsersDesktop%22%2C%22dateInterval%22%3A%22Monthly%22%2C%22dateStart%22%3A%222018-07%22%2C%22dateEnd%22%3A%222018-10%22%2C%22segments%22%3A%22-1000%22%7D\\">NetMarketShare</a></li>\\n</ul>\\n","showInResults":true,"tags":["babel","javascript","polyfill"]}')}}]);